<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>Setlistify Admin — Set up two-factor authentication</title>
    <style>
        body { font-family: sans-serif; max-width: 480px; margin: 5vh auto; }
        .error { color: #b00020; }
        .secret { font-family: monospace; background: #f0f0f0; padding: 0.5em; word-break: break-all; }
        .codes { font-family: monospace; background: #f0f0f0; padding: 1em; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 0.25em; }
        img { max-width: 240px; }
        input[type=text] { width: 100%; padding: 0.5em; box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0.5em; }
        button { margin-top: 1em; padding: 0.6em 1.2em; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Set up two-factor authentication</h1>
    <p>This account cannot be used until enrollment completes (docs/architecture.md §11). Scan the
        QR code with your authenticator app, then enter the current 6-digit code below.</p>

    {% if error is defined and error %}
        <p class="error">{{ error }}</p>
    {% endif %}

    <img src="{{ qr_data_uri }}" alt="TOTP QR code">

    <p>Or enter this secret manually:</p>
    <p class="secret">{{ secret }}</p>

    <p><strong>Save these backup codes now — they are shown only once.</strong> Each can be used
        once if you lose access to your authenticator app.</p>
    <div class="codes">
        {% for code in backup_codes %}
            <span>{{ code }}</span>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>

    <form method="post" action="{{ confirm_path }}">
        <label for="code">Code from your authenticator app</label>
        <input type="text" id="code" name="code" inputmode="numeric" pattern="[0-9]*" autocomplete="one-time-code" required autofocus>
        <button type="submit">Confirm and finish enrollment</button>
    </form>
</body>
</html>
